  "Name": "Dichroic",
  "Notes": "Long-pass dichroic, 50% edge placed at 580 nm\n\nCaveats:\n- Manufacturability is scored with MINT/MAXT (minimum and maximum layer thickness) at a low weight. A sensitivity term (SENS) would score robustness to thickness errors directly, but it needs second derivatives of the merit function and is not offered; MINT/MAXT keep layers depositable and have exact derivatives.\n- The edge is a crossing over the sampled band, so its position is only as well defined as the sampling: 33 points over 80 nm are 2.5 nm apart, and a crossing cannot be located better than the grid it is interpolated on.",
